---
description: Keep every Actor README focused on the product and free of competitor content
alwaysApply: true
---

# Actor documentation

- Never include competitor names, competitor Actor links, rival comparisons, rankings or comparative benchmark results in any README or Store-facing documentation.
- Document the Actor's features, inputs, output fields, real examples, known limits, setup and pricing.
- A request to compare scrapers authorizes testing and reporting to the user; it does not authorize publishing the comparison in an Actor README.
- Keep future competitive test results in local validation artifacts unless the user explicitly requests another destination.
